---
id: org.dxos.plugin.blocks
name: BlocksPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A block-based outliner where every bullet is a first-class ECHO object. Designed to losslessly absorb Tana Paste imports.

## Extensions

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |

## Types

```mdl
type TextSpan
  fields:
    kind: 'text'
    text: string
    marks?: ('bold' | 'italic' | 'highlight' | 'code')[]
```

```mdl
type RefSpan
  fields:
    kind: 'ref'
    target: Ref<Obj>          # any ECHO object; label resolved at render time
```

```mdl
type StructuredContent
  desc: ordered run of TextSpan | RefSpan; supports inline marks and live-name refs.
  literals: (TextSpan | RefSpan)[]
```

```mdl
type TagDef
  desc: stub for supertag definitions; expanded in a later increment.
  fields:
    name: string
```

```mdl
type Block
  desc: |
    The substrate node. Most fields optional and unused in Increment 1;
    defined now to be a faithful Tana-Paste import target without later migration.
  fields:
    content?: StructuredContent
    children?: Ref<Block>[]
    kind?: 'bullet' | 'heading' | 'todo' | 'image' | 'url' | 'search' | 'view' | 'code'
    tags?: Ref<TagDef>[]
    fields?: Record<string, Ref<Block>[]>
    state?: { checked?: boolean }
    view?: { kind: 'table' | 'cards' | 'tabs' | 'calendar' }
    attachment?: { kind: 'image' | 'file', url: string }
```

```mdl
type BlockOutline
  desc: navigator-openable container for a Block tree.
  fields:
    name?: string
    root: Ref<Block>
```

## Components

```mdl
component BlockArticle
  desc: |
    Article surface for a BlockOutline. Resolves the outline's root Block
    and mounts the BlockEditor. Falls back to a (loading...) message
    while the root ref is unresolved.
  props:
    role: string
    subject: BlockOutline
    attendableId: string
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │ <BlockEditor>           │
    └─────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component BlockEditor
  desc: |
    ProseMirror editor mounted over a single Block. Reads Block.content
    on mount, writes Block.content on every doc-changing transaction.
    Plain text in one paragraph; no marks, no inline refs, no nested
    children. External mutations into the editor are not synced
    (one-way: editor -> ECHO).
  props:
    block: Block
    autoFocus?: boolean
    onEnter?: (beforeText, afterText) -> void   # parent splits into a sibling
  emits:
    onEnter(beforeText: string, afterText: string)   # cursor split position
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │ contenteditable text…   │
    └─────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component BlockTree
  desc: |
    Renders the visible bullets of a BlockOutline as a flat list of
    BlockEditors. Holds the Enter-creates-sibling logic and a
    contextmenu listener that copies a bullet's DXN to the clipboard.
    The rootBlock is the (invisible) container; its children are the
    visible Blocks.
  props:
    rootBlock: Block
  state:
    focusId?: string                  # block id to autofocus after Enter
  actions:
    handleEnter(currentBlock, beforeText, afterText)
    handleContextMenu(event)          # copies Obj.getDXN(block) to clipboard
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────┐
    │ • bullet 1              │
    │ • bullet 2              │
    │ ...                     │
    └─────────────────────────┘
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Plugin scaffold
  req F-1.1: BlockOutline appears in the navigator's Create menu (gated under isLabs).
  req F-1.2: Creating a BlockOutline persists a BlockOutline + a single empty root Block in ECHO.
  req F-1.3: Opening a BlockOutline renders the BlockArticle placeholder without console errors.
  req F-1.4: Build, lint, and tests pass for plugin-blocks and composer-app.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Editable bullet      # Increment 2 (current)
  desc: |
    Single editable text bullet backed by a Block ECHO object. Out of
    scope: marks (bold/italic/highlight), inline refs (Increment 4),
    hierarchy (Increment 3), and syncing external mutations into the
    editor (deferred).
  req F-2.1: ProseMirror editor renders the root Block's content on mount.
  req F-2.2: Typing updates Block.content reactively; reload restores it.
  req F-2.3: Doc schema is one paragraph holding text*; no marks or ref nodes.
  req F-2.4:
    when: Block.content is empty or undefined
    then: editor mounts with an empty paragraph; cursor placeable; typing creates a single TextSpan.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Flat sibling bullets    # Increment 3 (current)
  desc: |
    The outline's root Block is invisible; its `children` array holds
    the visible bullets. Enter splits the current bullet at the cursor
    and inserts a new sibling. Each bullet has a stable DXN copyable
    via right-click. Out of scope here: Tab/Shift+Tab nesting (F-3b),
    drag-reorder, folding.
  req F-3.1:
    when: user presses Enter inside a bullet
    then:
      - current Block.content trimmed to the before-cursor text
      - new Block created with the after-cursor text as content
      - new Block ref spliced into rootBlock.children at currentIndex + 1
      - cursor lands at start of the new bullet
  req F-3.2: Each rendered bullet has a stable DXN derived from Obj.getDXN(block).
  req F-3.3:
    when: user right-clicks a bullet
    then: bullet's DXN is copied to the clipboard
  req F-3.4: I1/I2 outlines (root Block with content, no children) auto-migrate to root with one child Block on first mount.
```

```mdl
feat F-3b: Nested bullets         # Increment 3b (current)
  desc: |
    Bullets can be re-parented via Tab (indent under previous sibling) and
    Shift+Tab (dedent to grandparent's children). Rendering is recursive:
    each Block's children render indented below it. The moved Block's own
    children come along (indenting moves the whole subtree).
  req F-3b.1:
    when: user presses Tab inside a bullet that has a previous sibling
    then:
      - bullet's ref is removed from its parent's children
      - bullet's ref is appended to the previous sibling's children
      - bullet keeps its own children (subtree moves with it)
      - editor for the moved bullet regains focus after re-mount
  req F-3b.2:
    when: user presses Tab on the first child (no previous sibling)
    then: nothing happens; Tab is consumed (focus does not escape).
  req F-3b.3:
    when: user presses Shift+Tab inside a nested bullet
    then:
      - bullet's ref is removed from its parent's children
      - bullet's ref is inserted into its grandparent's children at parent's index + 1
      - editor for the moved bullet regains focus after re-mount
  req F-3b.4:
    when: user presses Shift+Tab on a top-level bullet (no grandparent)
    then: nothing happens; Shift+Tab is consumed.
```

```mdl
component BlockNode
  desc: |
    Recursive renderer. One BlockEditor for this Block, then a nested column
    of BlockNodes for its children. Tab/Shift+Tab/Enter handlers live here so
    they can close over the parent + grandparent context.
  props:
    block: Block
    parent: Block                       # who owns block via children[]
    grandparent?: Block                 # who owns parent
    focusId?: string
    setFocusId: (id?: string) -> void
  actions:
    handleEnter(beforeText, afterText)
    handleIndent()                      # Tab — re-parent under prev sibling
    handleDedent()                      # Shift+Tab — re-parent to grandparent
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Inline live-name refs    # Increment 4
  req F-4.1: Typing @ opens an object picker reusing plugin-markdown's useLinkQuery.
  req F-4.2: Selecting an object inserts a ref segment into Block.content.
  req F-4.3: The ref segment renders the target's current label; rename propagates.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Backlinks panel       # Increment 5
  req F-5.1: Any ECHO object surface displays a "Linked references" panel.
  req F-5.2: Panel lists incoming refs powered by db.query.referencedBy().
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Tags and fields       # Increment 6
  req F-6.1: A Block can be tagged via picker; TagDef is created on demand.
  req F-6.2: Tagged Block renders typed fields inline below the bullet.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Tana Paste import     # Increment 7
  req F-7.1: Pasting a payload starting with %%tana%% into a BlockOutline imports the structure as Blocks.
  req F-7.2: Supertags, fields, references, and dates are preserved using a stable-ID translation table.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Increment 1 — scaffold renders
  given: composer-app is running with isLabs enabled
  when: user creates a Block Outline from the navigator
  then:
    - BlockOutline + empty root Block appear in ECHO
    - BlockArticle surface renders the placeholder
    - no console errors
```

```mdl
test T-2: Increment 2 — editable bullet round-trips
  given: composer-app is running, a Block Outline has been created
  when: user types "hello world" into the editor and reloads the page
  then:
    - Block.content === [{ kind: 'text', text: 'hello world' }]
    - on reload, the editor mounts with "hello world" visible
    - no console errors attributable to plugin-blocks
```

```mdl
test T-3: Increment 3 — Enter creates a new sibling
  given: a Block Outline with a single bullet "first"
  when: user places cursor at end of "first" and presses Enter, then types "second"
  then:
    - rootBlock.children has two Block refs in order
    - first Block.content === [{ kind: 'text', text: 'first' }]
    - second Block.content === [{ kind: 'text', text: 'second' }]
    - on reload, both bullets render with original text
```

```mdl
test T-4: Increment 3 — DXN copy
  given: a Block Outline with a bullet, navigator.clipboard available
  when: user right-clicks the bullet
  then: Obj.getDXN(block) is written to the clipboard
```

```mdl
test T-5: Increment 3b — Tab indents
  given: an outline with two top-level bullets [A, B]
  when: cursor is in B and user presses Tab
  then:
    - rootBlock.children === [A] (B removed from top level)
    - A.children === [B] (B is now A's child)
    - B.children unchanged (B keeps its own subtree)
    - B's editor has focus after re-mount
```

```mdl
test T-6: Increment 3b — Shift+Tab dedents
  given: an outline where A.children === [B]
  when: cursor is in B and user presses Shift+Tab
  then:
    - A.children === [] (B removed from A)
    - rootBlock.children === [A, B] (B is now sibling of A)
    - B's editor has focus after re-mount
```

